I'll help you implement a typing animation effect for forms. Here's a practical solution using CSS:

## HTML + CSS Solution

### 1. Basic Implementation
```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<style>
.form-group {
  margin-bottom: 20px;
}

.form-control {
  padding: 10px;
  border: 2px solid #ddd;
  border-radius: 4px;
  font-size: 16px;
  width: 100%;
  transition: border-color 0.3s ease;
}

.form-control:focus {
  outline: none;
  border-color: #007bff;
  box-shadow: 0 0 0 2px rgba(0,123,255,0.25);
}

/* Typing animation */
@keyframes typing {
  0% { width: 0; }
  100% { width: 100%; }
}

@keyframes blink-caret {
  50% { border-color: transparent transparent; }
}

.typing-animation {
  overflow: hidden;
  border-right: 3px solid #007bff;
  white-space: nowrap;
  animation: 
    typing 3.5s steps(40, end),
    blink-caret 0.75s step-end infinite;
}

/* Alternative: Subtle input highlight */
@keyframes pulse {
  0% { box-shadow: 0 0 0 0 rgba(0,123,255,0.4); }
  70% { box-shadow: 0 0 0(0,123,255,0.4); }
  100% { box-shadow: 0 0 0 0 rgba(0,123,255,0.4); }
}

.input-focused {
  animation: pulse 1s ease-in-out;
}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<form id="myForm">
  <div class="form-group">
    <input type="text" class="form-control" placeholder="Name" id="name">
  </div>
  <div class="form-group">
    <input type="email" class="form-control" placeholder="Email" id="email">
  </div>
  <div class="form-group">
    <textarea class="form-control" placeholder="Message"></textarea>
  </div>
</form>

<script>
// Add subtle animation on focus
document.querySelectorAll('.form-control').forEach(input => {
  input.addEventListener('focus', function() {
    this.classList.add('input-focused');
    setTimeout(() => this.classList.remove('input-focused'), 1000);
  });
});

// Optional: Add typing indicator during form completion
let typingTimer;
document.querySelectorAll('.form-control').forEach(input => {
  input.addEventListener('input', function() {
    clearTimeout(typingTimer);
    this.classList.add('typing');
    typingTimer = setTimeout(() => {
      this.classList.remove('typing');
    }, 1000);
  });
});
</script>

</body>
</html>
```

### 2. Advanced Typing Indicator
```html
<div class="typing-indicator">
  <span></span><span></span><span></span>
</div>

<style>
.typing-indicator {
  display: none;
  margin-top: 10px;
}

.typing-active .typing-indicator {
  display: block;
}

.typing-indicator span {
  display: inline-block;
  width: 8px;
  height: 8px;
  background-color: #007bff;
  border-radius: 50%;
  margin: 0 2px;
  animation: typing-dot 1.4s infinite ease-in-out;
}

.typing-indicator span:nth-child(1) { animation-delay: -0.32s; }
.typing-indicator span:nth-child(2) { animation-delay: -0.16s; }

@keyframes typing-dot {
  0%, 80%, 100% { transform: scale(0); opacity: 0.5; }
  40% { transform: scale(1); opacity: 1; }
}
</style>
```

### 3. Form Progress Animation
```javascript
// Show progress as user fills form
function updateFormProgress() {
  const form = document.getElementById('myForm');
  const inputs = form.querySelectorAll('input, textarea');
  const filled = Array.from(inputs).filter(input => input.value.trim() !== '').length;
  const progress = (filled / inputs.length) * 100;

  // Update progress bar visually
  form.style.setProperty('--progress', `${progress}%`);
}

document.getElementById('myForm').addEventListener('input', updateFormProgress);
```

## Quick Implementation Steps:
1. Copy the CSS code into your stylesheet
2. Add the HTML structure to your form
3. Include the JavaScript for interactive effects
4. Customize colors and timing to match your design

The solution includes focus animations, typing indicators, and form progress feedback to enhance user experience during form completion.

